{
  "id": "set-cannot-complete",
  "description": "set may declare and rearrange work and may request legal transitions, and it may not author Done. A row asking for done on a todo with no committed verdict is refused; the same set's other rows, which only block, do not apply either, because a set is one transaction.",
  "decisions": [
    "The refusal names the row's label, not the whole set. A caller that mis-typed one row learns which one.",
    "The set is refused whole. Partially applying a multi-row set would leave the model's mental model of the plan wrong in a way no reply can correct, which is the defect ops.rs:1035 has today when it authors Done directly.",
    "A second set that asks only for blocked applies, which is the control: this fixture fails open if the driver simply refuses every set.",
    "There is no committed verdict anywhere in this plan, so no token can be forged into the refusal path by the test itself."
  ],
  "prompt": "Package the tarball and mark the packaging row done.",
